ck-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["SOLV Energy, Inc. is a mid-cap utilities business with a $5.6B market cap on $2.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are expanding by +3.8pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 10% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $310M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 12 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.22\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.7\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.6%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 67% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6676493176423435},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (22.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"SGA costs surged 65% YoY \u2014 may reflect legal, restructuring, or operational issues","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Utilities peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 9/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Utilities peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Utilities \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Financial quality scores above most Utilities peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"SOLV Energy (MWH) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/solv-energy-mwh-q3-2026-192913000.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794512195.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.153,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What To Expect From SOLV Energy Inc (MWH) Q3 2026 Earnings","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/expect-solv-energy-inc-mwh-123108638.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794400268.0,"origin":"tii